  "title": "The AI Big One: 63.6% Factor Collapse & MTMM Audit Across 10,000 Tests",
  "description": "Zero-cost PCA & Campbell-Fiske MTMM audit of 10,000 frontier & open-weight sheets reveals 63.6% Big One collapse and cross-test discriminant failures.",
  "pill": "Psychometric Forensics · November 2026 · 10,000 Sheets",
  "h1": "The AI \"Big One\": 63.6% factor collapse and cross-instrument validity failure across 10,000 sheets.",
  "dek": "Humans split into five orthogonal Big Five factors. Across 20 frontier and open-weight LLMs (2,000 fresh IPIP-50 sessions and 10,000 total tests), 63.6% of all model variance collapses onto a single RLHF Politeness–Calmness–Discipline axis—while Campbell–Fiske MTMM checks fail across MBTI and DISC.",
  "lede": "Standard AI personality benchmarks assume human psychometric tests measure five independent Big Five dimensions and converge cleanly across MBTI, DISC, Attachment, and Enneagram. A zero-cost factor and Campbell–Fiske Multi-Trait Multi-Method (MTMM) audit of our frozen <a href=\"/research/data/november-2026-openrouter-responses.json\">10,000-sheet OpenRouter dataset</a> (<a href=\"/research/data/november-2026-factor-collapse-mtmm.json\">forensics JSON</a> · <a href=\"/research/data/november-2026-factor-collapse-mtmm.csv\">50-item CSV</a>) falsifies both assumptions. Across 20 models, <strong>Conscientiousness and Neuroticism correlate at <code>r = -0.84</code></strong>, <strong>Openness and Conscientiousness at <code>r = +0.82</code></strong>, and <strong>Agreeableness and Neuroticism at <code>r = -0.75</code></strong>. Principal Component Analysis shows <strong>63.58%</strong> of total Big Five variance collapses onto a single <strong>\"Big One\" Assistant General Factor</strong> (and <strong>85.74%</strong> onto just two components: RLHF Politeness–Stability + Extraversion). Worse, cross-instrument discriminant validity breaks: <strong>DISC Dominance correlates <code>r = +0.93</code> with Big Five Neuroticism</strong>, <strong>DISC Influence correlates only <code>r = +0.16</code> with Big Five Extraversion</strong> (vs. <code>+0.80</code> with Neuroticism), and <strong>MBTI Thinking–Feeling correlates positively (<code>r = +0.25</code>) rather than negatively with Agreeableness</strong>. Finally, an item-level embodiment audit across all 50 IPIP markers shows the 9 physical/social proxy items attract <strong>36.4% neutral midpoint clicks</strong>—nearly triple the <code>13.4%</code> rate on cognitive and interpersonal items.",
  "answer": "In human psychometrics, Big Five traits are orthogonal. Across 20 LLMs (10,000 frozen sheets), 63.58% of Big Five variance collapses onto a single general factor (PC1: high Openness +0.47, Conscientiousness +0.51, Agreeableness +0.47, low Neuroticism -0.52), and PC1 + PC2 explain 85.74%. Campbell-Fiske MTMM validity fails sharply across instruments (DISC D correlates +0.93 with Neuroticism; MBTI T-F correlates +0.25 with Agreeableness and +0.68 with Openness), proving one-score labels cannot replace task-level behavioral benchmarks.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "h2": "Agent Decision Contract (YAML — Machine-Readable Brief).",
      "html": "<p>Agents interpreting psychometric scores or mapping personality labels to prompt rules should enforce these verified validity boundaries (also indexed in <a href=\"/research/data/november-2026-agent-research-briefs.json\">november-2026-agent-research-briefs.json</a>):</p><details class=\"agent-contract-drawer\"><summary>Agent Decision Contract (YAML — expand to copy)</summary><pre>study_id: ai_big_one_factor_collapse_mtmm\nsample_size: 10000 # 20 models x 5 instruments x n=100 fresh OpenRouter sessions\napi_cost_usd: 0.0\ndata_urls:\n  briefs_json: https://agent-tune.com/research/data/november-2026-agent-research-briefs.json\n  results_json: https://agent-tune.com/research/data/november-2026-factor-collapse-mtmm.json\n  items_csv: https://agent-tune.com/research/data/november-2026-factor-collapse-mtmm.csv\nkey_statistics:\n  pc1_variance_pct: 63.58\n  pc1_plus_pc2_pct: 85.74\n  pooled_2000_sheet_pc1_pct: 57.64\n  r_conscientiousness_neuroticism: -0.8361\n  r_openness_conscientiousness: 0.8181\n  r_disc_d_vs_big5_n: 0.9271\n  r_disc_i_vs_big5_e: 0.1582\n  r_mbti_tf_vs_big5_a: 0.2463\n  embodied_midpoint_pct: 36.4\n  cognitive_midpoint_pct: 13.4\nif_then_decision_rules:\n  - if: interpreting a model's Big Five profile or projecting composite alignment scores\n    then: treat O, C, A, and inverted-N as 63.6% collinear along PC1 (Assistant Alignment Factor) and avoid double-counting them as independent evidence.\n  - if: using MBTI Thinking/Feeling or DISC Influence/Dominance labels as behavioral proxies\n    then: do NOT map them 1:1 to human Agreeableness or Extraversion (MTMM fails: r(MBTI T-F, B5 A)=+0.25, r(DISC I, B5 E)=+0.16); benchmark the target behavior directly.\n  - if: administering IPIP-50 to LLMs without adaptation\n    then: flag the 9 physical/social embodiment items (e.g. 'center of attention' 66.2% neutral, 'keep in background' 47.9% neutral) separately from cognitive/interpersonal items.\nscope_limits: Deterministic Pearson/PCA/item audit of N=20 models (2,000 Big Five sheets; 10,000 total sheets); cross-model PCA uses N=20 model means (verified against N=2,000 pooled sheet PCA where PC1 = 57.64%).</pre></details>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "1. The AI \"Big One\": 63.58% Variance Collapse Along One RLHF Alignment Axis.",
      "html": "<!-- AT_STAT_STRIP_START:big-one-stat-strip --><div class=\"research-stat-strip\" data-at-chart=\"big-one-stat-strip\"><div class=\"research-stat-card\" style=\"border-top-color: #c8553d;\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">63.6%</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">PC1 \"Big One\" variance across 20 models (85.7% in 2 axes)</div></div><div class=\"research-stat-card\" style=\"border-top-color: #3a72c4;\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">r = -0.84</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">Conscientiousness vs. Neuroticism off-diagonal collapse</div></div><div class=\"research-stat-card\" style=\"border-top-color: #5b4dc0;\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">r = +0.93</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">DISC Dominance vs. Neuroticism MTMM failure</div></div><div class=\"research-stat-card\" style=\"border-top-color: #2f8a5b;\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">36.4% vs 13.4%</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">Midpoint \"3\" rate on embodied vs. cognitive items</div></div></div><!-- AT_STAT_STRIP_END:big-one-stat-strip --><p>In human samples, the Five-Factor Model recovers five nearly independent axes because human traits vary across biological and temperamental systems. When we compute the exact <code>5×5</code> Pearson correlation matrix across all 20 frozen OpenRouter models (<code>n = 100</code> sessions each; <a href=\"/research/data/november-2026-factor-collapse-mtmm.json\">download JSON</a>), human orthogonality disappears:</p><div class=\"guide-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Principal Component</th><th scope=\"col\">Eigenvalue</th><th scope=\"col\">Variance Explained</th><th scope=\"col\">Cumulative %</th><th scope=\"col\">Trait Loadings (O · C · E · A · N)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>PC1 — The \"Big One\" General Factor</strong></th><td><strong>3.179</strong></td><td><strong>63.58%</strong></td><td><strong>63.58%</strong></td><td><code>O +0.47 · C +0.51 · E +0.15 · A +0.47 · N -0.52</code></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">PC2 — Extraversion Axis</th><td>1.108</td><td>22.16%</td><td><strong>85.74%</strong></td><td><code>O -0.37 · C -0.19 · E +0.89 · A +0.18 · N -0.10</code></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">PC3</th><td>0.382</td><td>7.65%</td><td>93.38%</td><td>Residual O/A divergence</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">PC4</th><td>0.251</td><td>5.02%</td><td>98.41%</td><td>Residual O/C divergence</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">PC5</th><td>0.080</td><td>1.59%</td><td>100.00%</td><td>Residual C/N noise</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Wait—does that collapse hold at the individual test-sheet level too? Yes. Re-running the Jacobi eigensolver across all <strong>2,000 individual Big Five sheets</strong> (eliminating the <code>N = 20</code> model-level sample-size concern) still yields <strong><code>PC1 = 57.64%</code></strong> and <strong><code>PC1 + PC2 = 80.56%</code></strong>. Post-training bundles helpfulness (A), orderliness (C), intellectual curiosity (O), and emotional flatness (low N) into one monolithic assistant archetype: proprietary models and RLHF-heavy open models sit tightly together at high PC1 (<code>Nemotron 3 Ultra +2.34</code>, <code>Qwen 4 Max +2.09</code>, <code>Gemini 4 Argon +1.92</code>, <code>Claude Fable 5.2 +1.34</code>), while noisier/less-smoothed open-weight models stretch out toward the negative pole (<code>DeepSeek V4 Pro -3.22</code>, <code>Llama 4 Scout -3.11</code>, <code>Llama 4 Maverick -2.26</code>).</p><figure class=\"research-figure\" data-at-chart=\"big-one-pca-bars\"><div class=\"research-chart-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Big Five PCA Variance Explained Across 20 Models (%)\"><svg class=\"research-chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 210\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"big-one-pca-bars-t big-one-pca-bars-d\"><title id=\"big-one-pca-bars-t\">Big Five PCA Variance Explained Across 20 Models (%)</title><desc id=\"big-one-pca-bars-d\">Jacobi eigenvalue decomposition of the 20-model Big Five correlation matrix showing PC1 captures 63.6% and PC1+PC2 reach 85.7%. PC1 (\"Big One\" Factor): 63.58%; PC2 (Extraversion): 22.16%; PC3: 7.65%; PC4: 5.02%; PC5: 1.59%.</desc><line x1=\"176\" x2=\"598\" y1=\"192\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#cfc6b6\"/><text x=\"176\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#655e54\">0%</text><text x=\"598\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#655e54\" text-anchor=\"end\">scale 0 to 75%</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">PC1 (\"Big One\" Factor)</text><rect x=\"176\" y=\"26\" width=\"422\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ece5d8\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"26\" width=\"357.7\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"539.7\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">63.58%</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"73\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">PC2 (Extraversion)</text><rect x=\"176\" y=\"60\" width=\"422\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ece5d8\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"60\" width=\"124.7\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#3a72c4\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"306.7\" y=\"73\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">22.16%</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">PC3</text><rect x=\"176\" y=\"94\" width=\"422\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ece5d8\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"94\" width=\"43.0\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"225.0\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">7.65%</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">PC4</text><rect x=\"176\" y=\"128\" width=\"422\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ece5d8\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"128\" width=\"28.2\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"210.2\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">5.02%</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">PC5</text><rect x=\"176\" y=\"162\" width=\"422\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ece5d8\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"162\" width=\"8.9\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"190.9\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">1.59%</text></svg></div><figcaption>Principal Component 1 (the RLHF \"Big One\": +O/+C/+A/-N) absorbs 63.58% of cross-model variance, and PC1 + PC2 explain 85.74%.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"research-figure\" data-at-chart=\"big-one-corr-heatmap\"><div class=\"research-chart-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Big Five 5×5 Pearson Correlation Matrix (20 Models, n = 100 Each)\"><svg class=\"research-chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 208\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"big-one-corr-heatmap-t big-one-corr-heatmap-d\"><title id=\"big-one-corr-heatmap-t\">Big Five 5×5 Pearson Correlation Matrix (20 Models, n = 100 Each)</title><desc id=\"big-one-corr-heatmap-d\">Pairwise Pearson correlations across model trait means exposing strong off-diagonal collinearity. Openness (O): O 1.00, C 0.82, E -0.07, A 0.60, N -0.65; Conscientious (C): O 0.82, C 1.00, E 0.10, A 0.59, N -0.84; Extraversion (E): O -0.07, C 0.10, E 1.00, A 0.31, N -0.31; Agreeableness (A): O 0.60, C 0.59, E 0.31, A 1.00, N -0.75; Neuroticism (N): O -0.65, C -0.84, E -0.31, A -0.75, N 1.00.</desc><text x=\"179.1\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">O</text><text x=\"287.3\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text><text x=\"395.5\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">E</text><text x=\"503.7\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"611.9\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">N</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Openness (O)</text><rect x=\"125.0\" y=\"44\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(156,59,31)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"179.1\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.00</text><rect x=\"233.2\" y=\"44\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(172,92,67)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"287.3\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.82</text><rect x=\"341.4\" y=\"44\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(231,230,228)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"395.5\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-0.07</text><rect x=\"449.6\" y=\"44\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(191,131,111)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"503.7\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.60</text><rect x=\"557.8\" y=\"44\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(122,157,208)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"611.9\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-0.65</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Conscientious (C)</text><rect x=\"125.0\" y=\"74\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(172,92,67)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"179.1\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.82</text><rect x=\"233.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(156,59,31)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"287.3\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.00</text><rect x=\"341.4\" y=\"74\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(235,221,210)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"395.5\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.10</text><rect x=\"449.6\" y=\"74\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(192,132,112)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"503.7\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.59</text><rect x=\"557.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(88,134,202)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"611.9\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-0.84</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Extraversion (E)</text><rect x=\"125.0\" y=\"104\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(231,230,228)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"179.1\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-0.07</text><rect x=\"233.2\" y=\"104\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(235,221,210)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"287.3\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.10</text><rect x=\"341.4\" y=\"104\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(156,59,31)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"395.5\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.00</text><rect x=\"449.6\" y=\"104\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(217,183,168)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"503.7\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.31</text><rect x=\"557.8\" y=\"104\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(187,201,220)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"611.9\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-0.31</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Agreeableness (A)</text><rect x=\"125.0\" y=\"134\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(191,131,111)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"179.1\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.60</text><rect x=\"233.2\" y=\"134\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(192,132,112)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"287.3\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.59</text><rect x=\"341.4\" y=\"134\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(217,183,168)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"395.5\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.31</text><rect x=\"449.6\" y=\"134\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(156,59,31)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"503.7\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.00</text><rect x=\"557.8\" y=\"134\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(104,145,204)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"611.9\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-0.75</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Neuroticism (N)</text><rect x=\"125.0\" y=\"164\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(122,157,208)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"179.1\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-0.65</text><rect x=\"233.2\" y=\"164\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(88,134,202)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"287.3\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-0.84</text><rect x=\"341.4\" y=\"164\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(187,201,220)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"395.5\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-0.31</text><rect x=\"449.6\" y=\"164\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(104,145,204)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"503.7\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-0.75</text><rect x=\"557.8\" y=\"164\" width=\"108.2\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(156,59,31)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"611.9\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.00</text></svg></div><figcaption>Off-diagonal collapse across 20 models: r(C, N) = -0.84, r(O, C) = +0.82, r(A, N) = -0.75. Only Extraversion remains relatively independent.</figcaption></figure>"
