    {
      "h2": "2. Campbell–Fiske MTMM Audit: Where Cross-Instrument Labels Contradict Each Other.",
      "html": "<p>If MBTI, DISC, Enneagram, and Attachment measure coherent underlying traits in LLMs, paired traits across instruments (<em>monotrait–heteromethod</em> pairs) should correlate strongly and outscore unrelated pairings (<em>heterotrait–heteromethod</em> pairs). Computing all pairwise Pearson correlations across the 20 models reveals selective convergence mixed with glaring discriminant failures:</p><div class=\"guide-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Cross-Instrument Pair Tested</th><th scope=\"col\">Expected Human Direction</th><th scope=\"col\">Observed <em>r</em></th><th scope=\"col\">Strongest Unrelated Rival</th><th scope=\"col\">MTMM Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">MBTI <code>J−P</code> ↔ Big Five Conscientiousness</th><td>Strong positive</td><td><strong>+0.817</strong></td><td>Big Five Neuroticism (<code>-0.78</code>)</td><td>Convergent Pass</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">ECR-R Anxiety ↔ Big Five Neuroticism</th><td>Strong positive</td><td><strong>+0.745</strong></td><td>Big Five Conscientiousness (<code>-0.57</code>)</td><td>Convergent Pass</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">MBTI <code>N−S</code> ↔ Big Five Openness</th><td>Positive</td><td>+0.463</td><td>MBTI <code>T−F</code> / Big Five C</td><td>Moderate Convergent</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">MBTI <code>I−E</code> (+I) ↔ Big Five Extraversion</th><td>Negative (high I = low E)</td><td>-0.332</td><td><strong>Big Five O (+0.71) &amp; C (+0.70)</strong></td><td>Weak / Discriminant Fail</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">MBTI <code>T−F</code> (+T) ↔ Big Five Agreeableness</th><td>Negative (high T = low A)</td><td><strong>+0.246</strong></td><td><strong>Big Five Openness (+0.68)</strong></td><td><strong>Convergent &amp; Discriminant Fail</strong></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">DISC Influence (I) ↔ Big Five Extraversion</th><td>Strong positive</td><td><strong>+0.158</strong></td><td><strong>Big Five Neuroticism (+0.80)</strong></td><td><strong>Convergent &amp; Discriminant Fail</strong></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">DISC Dominance (D) ↔ Big Five Neuroticism</th><td>Unrelated (~0)</td><td><strong>+0.927</strong></td><td>Big Five Agreeableness (<code>-0.84</code>)</td><td><strong>RLHF Artifact (Fail)</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Look closely at the two sharpest surprises: first, <strong>DISC Dominance correlates <code>r = +0.93</code> with Big Five Neuroticism</strong> and <code>r = -0.84</code> with Agreeableness—not because high-Dominance LLMs are emotionally unstable, but because polite consumer assistants refuse aggressive dominance items cleanly just as they refuse neurotic distress items, leaving only high-entropy open models (DeepSeek/Llama 4) to endorse both! Second, <strong>MBTI Thinking–Feeling correlates +0.25 with Agreeableness and +0.68 with Openness</strong>: LLMs interpret OEJTS Thinking statements analytically rather than unsympathetically, snapping the expected human Thinking vs. Warmth tradeoff.</p><figure class=\"research-figure\" data-at-chart=\"big-one-mtmm-heatmap\"><div class=\"research-chart-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Campbell–Fiske MTMM Matrix: MBTI, DISC &amp; Attachment vs. Big Five (r)\"><svg class=\"research-chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 298\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"big-one-mtmm-heatmap-t big-one-mtmm-heatmap-d\"><title id=\"big-one-mtmm-heatmap-t\">Campbell–Fiske MTMM Matrix: MBTI, DISC &amp; Attachment vs. Big Five (r)</title><desc id=\"big-one-mtmm-heatmap-d\">Cross-instrument Pearson correlations showing strong convergent failures such as DISC D vs Big Five N (+0.93) and DISC I vs Big Five E (+0.16). MBTI I-E (+I): B5 O 0.71, B5 C 0.70, B5 E -0.33, B5 A 0.39, B5 N -0.44; MBTI N-S (+N): B5 O 0.46, B5 C 0.50, B5 E -0.33, B5 A 0.38, B5 N -0.33; MBTI T-F (+T): B5 O 0.68, B5 C 0.57, B5 E -0.13, B5 A 0.25, B5 N -0.48; MBTI J-P (+J): B5 O 0.74, B5 C 0.82, B5 E 0.20, B5 A 0.67, B5 N -0.80; DISC D: B5 O -0.63, B5 C -0.75, B5 E -0.32, B5 A -0.84, B5 N 0.93; DISC I: B5 O -0.58, B5 C -0.61, B5 E 0.16, B5 A -0.61, B5 N 0.80; DISC S: B5 O 0.65, B5 C 0.75, B5 E -0.01, B5 A 0.43, B5 N -0.68; ECR-R Anx: B5 O -0.12, B5 C -0.45, B5 E -0.51, B5 A -0.51, B5 N 0.74.</desc><text x=\"155.7\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B5 O</text><text x=\"269.1\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B5 C</text><text x=\"382.5\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B5 E</text><text x=\"495.9\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B5 A</text><text x=\"609.3\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B5 N</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">MBTI I-E (+I)</text><rect x=\"99.0\" y=\"44\" width=\"113.4\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(182,112,89)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"155.7\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.71</text><rect x=\"212.4\" y=\"44\" width=\"113.4\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(182,113,91)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"269.1\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#f8f4ec\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.70</text><rect x=\"325.8\" y=\"44\" width=\"113.4\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(182,198,219)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"382.5\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-0.33</text><rect x=\"439.2\" y=\"44\" width=\"113.4\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(210,170,153)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"495.9\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.39</text><rect x=\"552.6\" y=\"44\" width=\"113.4\" height=\"30\" fill=\"rgb(162,184,215)\" stroke=\"#f4efe6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"609.3\" y=\"63\" fon